
Alessandro Nai, Max Grömping, and Dominique Wirz co-edited the recently published Elgar Encyclopedia of Political Communication (https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035301447). The encyclopedia serves as a reference work on the field of political communication, including media studies and journalism studies, presenting an authoritative overview of its key foundational theories and empirical methodologies. Authored by 581 contributors from 58 countries, its 431 entries explore diverse areas of inquiry, foreshadowing future trends and avenues for research.
The introductory chapter ‘Mapping political communication’ is available open access here: https://www.elgaronline.com/display/book/9781035301447/front-7.xml 